<section class="layout-container">

    <section id="anti-ragging">
        <!--Overall Heading-->
        <div class="generic-heading__row ">

            <div class="generic-heading__title-group">
                <h3>Bright Nursing's Anti&#8209;Ragging Policy</h3>
            </div>

            <div class="__divider">
                <div class="__line"></div>
                <div class="__dot"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!--Sub-Heading-->
        <div class="section-heading__title">
            <h4>Introduction</h4>
        </div>

        <p>
            The institution maintains an uncompromising <strong>zero-tolerance policy</strong> towards all forms of
            ragging, both
            within and outside of the campus premises. Ragging is a recognized offense and is strictly prohibited. Any
            violation will attract stringent disciplinary action as per Institutional Rules &amp; Regulations.
        </p>

        <!--Sub-Heading-->
        <div class="section-heading__title">
            <h4>What Constitutes as Ragging?</h4>
        </div>

        <p>
            Ragging includes, but is not limited to any act, conduct, and behaviour that causes physical, psychological,
            sexual or emotional harm, discomfort, ot fear to a student. This applies within or outside campus premises,
            including hostels, places of clinical and community training and online platforms.
        </p>

        <ul class="li-bullet">
            <li><strong>Acts of Violence</strong> and use of force against any students or any teachers and staff
                members.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Instigation &amp; Criminal Collusion:</strong> Direct or indirect involvement in promoting,
                planning
                or assisting in ragging in any manner whatsoever.</li>
            <li><strong>Public Nuisance</strong> casuing disruption of academic activities, public order and
                institutional decorum.</li>
            <li><strong>Unlawful Assembly &amp; Rioting:</strong> Any form of collective or organized involvement in
                ragging or misconduct.</li>
            <li><strong>Forcing</strong> and <strong>consumption</strong> of any kinds of alcohol or substance.</li>
            <li><strong>Sexually</strong> explicit comments and gestures.</li>
            <li><strong>Inappropiate</strong> Physical contact and advances.</li>
            <li><strong>Online harrasment</strong> via social media or messaging platforms.</li>
        </ul>

        <!--Sub-Heading-->
        <div class="section-heading__title">
            <h4>Penalties and Punishments for Ragging</h4>
        </div>

        <ul class="li-bullet">
            <li>Suspension for a specified period, or in severe cases, rustication from the Institution.
            </li>
            <li>Witholding of scholarships, results and other benefits.</li>
            <li>Prohibition from Examinations and Evaluation.</li>
            <li>Fines ranging from <strong>&#8377;25&comma;000</strong> to <strong>&#8377;1&comma;00&comma;000</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>In severe cases the offence may lead upto imprisonment upto 3 years.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <!--Heading-->
    <div class="generic-heading__row ">

        <div class="generic-heading__title-group">
            <h3>Code Of Conduct</h3>
